Design for Refill at Home is a design strategy focused on enabling consumers to refill products at home, reducing the need for single-use packaging and promoting a more sustainable consumption pattern. This strategy emphasizes the importance of designing products that are easy to refill and use, encouraging consumers to actively participate in the circular economy by extending the lifespan of products through refill options. By integrating refill mechanisms into product design, companies can not only reduce packaging waste but also foster a sense of ownership and responsibility among consumers towards the products they use. Research has shown that refill systems can significantly reduce environmental impacts by decreasing the demand for virgin materials and minimizing waste generation (Bocken et al., 2016). Moreover, offering refill options at home can enhance customer engagement and loyalty, leading to long-term business benefits for companies embracing this design strategy.